{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/text\/kerning(_:)"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"nonisolated","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kerning","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kerning","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CGFloat","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14CoreFoundation7CGFloatV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Text","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI4TextV","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"kerning","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The spacing to use between individual characters in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this text. Value of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":" sets the kerning to the system default value."}]}]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Return Value","level":2,"anchor":"return-value","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Text with the specified amount of kerning."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Kerning defines the offset, in points, that a text view should shift"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"characters from the default spacing. Use positive kerning to widen the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spacing between characters. Use negative kerning to tighten the spacing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between characters."}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["VStack(alignment: .leading) {","    Text(\"ABCDEF\").kerning(-3)","    Text(\"ABCDEF\")","    Text(\"ABCDEF\").kerning(3)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The last character in the first case, which uses negative kerning,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"experiences cropping because the kerning affects the trailing edge of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the text view as well."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Kerning attempts to maintain ligatures. For example, the Hoefler Text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"font uses a ligature for the letter combination "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ffl"}]},{"type":"text","text":", as in the word"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"raffle"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", shown here with a small negative and a small positive kerning:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ffl"}]},{"type":"text","text":" letter combination keeps a constant shape as the other letters"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"move together or apart. Beyond a certain point in either direction,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"however, kerning does disable nonessential ligatures."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"important","type":"aside","name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you add both the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Text\/tracking(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Text\/kerning(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" modifiers to a view, the view applies the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracking and ignores the kerning."}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kerning"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14CoreFoundation7CGFloatV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"CGFloat"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI4TextV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Text"}],"modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI4TextV7kerningyAC14CoreFoundation7CGFloatVF","extendedModule":"OpenSwiftUI","roleHeading":"Instance Method","title":"kerning(_:)","role":"symbol"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Text"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets the spacing, or kerning, between characters."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Text\/kerning(_:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/Text":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Text","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/text","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Text","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A view that displays one or more lines of read-only text."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Text","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","role":"collection","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"title":"OpenSwiftUI","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/Text/kerning(_:)":{"abstr